A||||2||GodSend||Distributor o-ring question||||1||
Z||000000||GodSend||10-19-2001||10:02 AM||||Well, tomorrow is the big day.  New o-ring, new egr tube, and new dog-bone.  I am going to replace the egr tube when the dist. is removed (to put the o-ring in).<P>I have been looking over all the online docs about removing the dist. , but I want to clarify something.<P>I am going to remove the dist. cap.  I will mark the exact location of the dist. on the block and also where the rotor is pointing.<P>Apparently when you lift the dist. out the rotor will turn, and you are to mark the new rotor location (I will call this point 2). <P>Now for a a few questions. If I am lifting the dist up and the rotor turns, when will it stop turning?  Once I have totally removed the dist?  Secondly.  When putting the dist back on, you point the rotor to Point 2, and when you push it down does it rotate back to the origional point you marked?  <P>Thanks guys, I am trying to do this without having to re-time my car because I am going in for a tune up in a few weeks anyways.  If I can get by till then, then I will be happy.  Cheers<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||10-19-2001||10:34 AM||||You've got it.<P>The distrubutor has a Helical gear on its shaft.  Consequently it will turn as it disengages from the camshaft gear.  As you lift the distributor the rotor will turn until it clears the camshaft gear.  When re-installing the distributor it will turn back in the oposite direction when it engages the camshaft gear.<P>So, mark the position of the rotor relative to the distributor backing plate and mark the location of the distributor relative to the intake manifold.  You should be able to reinstall to the original position with a little care.<P>Good luck||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fie Ro||10-19-2001||01:17 PM||||I did this last weekend and it isn't hard to do. Just be careful and precise with the marking points. If I where you I also should replace the pick-up coil while the distributor is out. I also looked at the gathered information before I did the job, it's good to know WHAT you're doing! ;-)<P>good luck,<BR>Roderick<P>------------------<BR>-The Beauty & The Beast-<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero GT & <BR>1977 Dodge W200||||reg||1
